This "ambiguity" must relate to some ancient compilers accepting '=3D-'
as an alias for '-=3D'. That must predate K&R 1st edition (1978), which
clearly defines the assignment operator syntax for operator 'op' as
'op=3D' [1].

But well, it's always good to eliminate warnings, so

Reviewed-by: Martin Wilck <mwilck@suse.com>

